IMPORT prelude

-- Lightweight math helpers that complement the stock prelude.
-- Extend this file as additional OPM numeric functions (Ln, Log, etc.)
-- become required by downstream translators such as opm2l4.

§ `Math`

§§ `Constants`

DECLARE EULER IS A NUMBER
@nlg Euler's number
EULER MEANS 2.718281828459045

DECLARE TAN_EPSILON IS A NUMBER
@nlg the tolerance below which a cosine counts as zero
TAN_EPSILON MEANS 0.000000001

§§ `Exponential & Logarithmic`

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg e raised to the power of %x%
exp x MEANS EXPONENT EULER x

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
@nlg the natural logarithm of %x%
ln x MEANS
  IF x AT MOST 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST (LN x)

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
@nlg the base-10 logarithm of %x%
log10 x MEANS
  IF x AT MOST 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST (LOG10 x)

§§ `Roots & Absolute Value`

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
sqrt x @nlg the square root of %x%
  MEANS IF x LESS THAN 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST (SQRT x)

GIVEN value IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
absNumber value @nlg the absolute value of %value%
  MEANS IF value LESS THAN 0 THEN 0 MINUS value ELSE value

§§ `Trigonometry`

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
@nlg the sine of %x%
sin x MEANS JUST (SIN x)

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
@nlg the cosine of %x%
cos x MEANS JUST (COS x)

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
@nlg the tangent of %x%
tan x MEANS
  IF absNumber (COS x) LESS THAN TAN_EPSILON
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (TAN x)

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
@nlg the arcsine of %x%
asin x MEANS
  IF x LESS THAN 0 MINUS 1
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF x GREATER THAN 1 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST (ASIN x)

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
@nlg the arccosine of %x%
acos x MEANS
  IF x LESS THAN 0 MINUS 1
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF x GREATER THAN 1 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST (ACOS x)

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
@nlg the arctangent of %x%
atan x MEANS JUST (ATAN x)
